<Page
  title="Waymark pass promise"
  description="Waymark's money-back pass promise. Full terms will be published here before it applies to any purchase."
  heading="Pass promise"
  lead="If you follow the plan, reach our readiness standard and still don't pass, we will refund what you paid for Waymark."
>
  <p class="note">
    The pass promise is not active yet. Payments open at launch, and the final terms will be published on this page
    before the promise applies to any purchase. No purchase made before then is covered.
  </p>

  <h2>How we expect it to work</h2>
  <p>These are the terms we are planning. They may change before launch, and the published version will apply.</p>
  <ol>
    <li>You bought Waymark Standard or Plus.</li>
    <li>Before your test, Waymark showed your readiness as "Likely to pass" and you completed at least two timed mock exams.</li>
    <li>You took the official Life in the UK test within a set time after reaching that standard.</li>
    <li>You did not pass, and you contact us within a set time after your test with evidence of the result.</li>
  </ol>
  <p>
    If all the conditions are met, we refund the price you paid for Waymark. The promise does not cover the official
    test fee or any other costs.
  </p>

  <h2>Why it has conditions</h2>
  <p>
    The promise is there to show we stand behind the plan. It works when the plan is followed: regular practice, timed
    mocks, and a readiness estimate based on enough evidence.
  </p>

  <p>Questions? Email <a href="mailto:support@waymarkprep.co.uk">support@waymarkprep.co.uk</a>.</p>
</Page>
